@startuml rag-builder
' IndexBuilder (sequential) vs ParallelIndexBuilder (rayon): both share ONE
' embedder and ONE summarizer, whose &self methods are thread-safe. Colour:
'   #6A1B9A purple = retrieval / build control   #2E7D32 green = neural workers
'   #00838F teal   = the resulting index          #455A64 grey  = corpus I/O
' `linetype ortho` is deliberately NOT set here: the two build paths converge on
' one shared pair of workers, and diagonal routing keeps those edges legible. The
' workers container uses a LIGHT fill (the rag-hnsw idiom) so the edge label
' drawn across it stays legible.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/rag-builder.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/rag/builder.md §3.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 40
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Index construction — sequential and data-parallel

rectangle "**Corpus**\nscan_directory: .txt · .md · .html  (one level, non-recursive)\nor a Vec<DocumentBuilder> supplied by the caller" as corpus #455A64

rectangle "**IndexBuilder**  //sequential//\n\nfor each builder:\n   id ← index.allocate_id()\n   doc ← process_builder(builder, id)\n   index.add_document(doc)\n   progress(i+1, total) every progress_interval = 100" as seq #6A1B9A

rectangle "**ParallelIndexBuilder**  //rayon//\n\nbuilders.**into_par_iter()**.map(|b| {\n   id ← DocumentId(next_id.fetch_add(1, Relaxed))\n   embed  ‖  summarise\n   b.build(id, synopsis, embedding)\n}).collect::<Vec<Result<Document>>>()" as par #6A1B9A

rectangle "<color:#1B5E20>**Shared neural workers** — both take &self" as workers #E8F5E9 {
  rectangle "**ModernBertEmbedder**\nembed_document(title, content) → Vec<f32>" as emb #2E7D32
  rectangle "**Summarizer**\ncreate_synopsis(explicit, content) → Synopsis\nfrom_model(embedder.model_arc())" as sum #2E7D32
}

rectangle "**Serial drain**\nfor doc in results: index.add_document(doc)?\n//needs &mut self//" as drain #6A1B9A

rectangle "**RagIndex<ExactCosineBackend>**" as index #00838F

corpus -down-> seq
corpus -down-> par

seq -right-> emb
seq -right-> sum
par -right-> emb
par -right-> sum

emb -[#2E7D32]down-> sum : **model_arc()**\n//shared Arc<ModernBertModel>//

seq -down-> index : add_document
par -down-> drain : Vec<Result<Document>>
drain -down-> index

note bottom of workers
  Both builders take **&self**, not &mut self, so every
  rayon worker shares **one** embedder and **one**
  summarizer. The 149 M-parameter ModernBERT weights
  are held once behind an ""Arc"": memory is Θ(1) in the
  thread count, not Θ(p).
end note

note right of drain
  The ""map"" is parallel; the drain is **serial**, because
  ""add_document"" needs ""&mut self"". With embedding-
  dominated work (f ≈ 0.95) Amdahl still yields ≈ 9× on
  16 cores — the serial tail is one ""HashMap"" insert plus
  one matrix-row push per document.
end note

note left of seq
  **IDs differ by construction path.**
  sequential ⇒ ""index.allocate_id()""
  parallel   ⇒ an ""AtomicU32"" counter from 0
  ""extend_index"" instead derives ids from
  ""index.len() + added"", which **collides**
  when the index has holes from removals.
end note
@enduml
